WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.982 --> 00:00:05.262
Tom Lindqvist: Morning, Vanessa. How's Tampa treating you?

2
00:00:06.603 --> 00:00:11.104
Vanessa Grant: Good, good. Traffic on 275 was actually moving today, so I'll take it.

3
00:00:12.032 --> 00:00:17.924
Tom Lindqvist: Ha. Small wins. Before we get into it, how's the Amazon Connect side holding up?

4
00:00:19.245 --> 00:00:28.463
Vanessa Grant: Yeah, it's been solid. We're seeing maybe 2,800 calls a week across the 64 showrooms, which is about where we were in August.

5
00:00:28.463 --> 00:00:38.884
Vanessa Grant: The AI Voice Agent is handling the store-hours and and order-status stuff, so the queue's been lighter. But hey, that's not why I asked for this.

6
00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:40.590
Tom Lindqvist: Right. What's going on?

7
00:00:40.813 --> 00:00:49.143
Vanessa Grant: So we redid the checkout flow. It's a single-page app now, which is a whole thing our devs are proud of.

8
00:00:49.143 --> 00:00:52.317
Vanessa Grant: And something's off with um, the tracking numbers.

9
00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.145
Tom Lindqvist: You know, Off how?

10
00:00:55.433 --> 00:01:12.527
Vanessa Grant: The dynamic number insertion just stops swapping. After someone navigates within the app, the number on the page stays whatever it was when the page first loaded. So if they click through to checkout and then call, it's the original number, not the campaign one.

11
00:01:13.674 --> 00:01:18.002
Tom Lindqvist: Okay. Um, and you're seeing that in the reports as...

12
00:01:19.456 --> 00:01:28.497
Vanessa Grant: As direct traffic. Calls from the new checkout are showing up as direct, no campaign, no keyword. Which makes the whole attribution thing useless for that flow.

13
00:01:28.497 --> 00:01:33.186
Vanessa Grant: We're talking maybe a couple hundred calls a month landing in the wrong bucket.

14
00:01:34.599 --> 00:01:39.821
Tom Lindqvist: Got it. Is this only on the checkout path, or are you seeing it elsewhere?

15
00:01:40.645 --> 00:01:47.330
Vanessa Grant: Honestly, mostly checkout. The rest of the site is fine. But checkout is where the money is, so.

16
00:01:47.799 --> 00:01:55.526
Tom Lindqvist: Yeah, that makes sense. Let me ask a couple things so I can get this in front of the right folks.

17
00:01:55.526 --> 00:01:58.102
Tom Lindqvist: When did the new checkout go live?

18
00:01:59.371 --> 00:02:09.679
Vanessa Grant: Uh, two weeks ago? The 2nd, I think. Our dev lead, Marcus, pushed it. Actually, wait, Marcus is on vacation, so it was his team.

19
00:02:10.595 --> 00:02:15.667
Tom Lindqvist: Like, okay. And are you seeing it on both mobile and desktop?

20
00:02:16.328 --> 00:02:19.464
Vanessa Grant: Yeah, both. Mobile's worse, but that's probably just volume.

21
00:02:20.335 --> 00:02:31.379
Tom Lindqvist: Alright. I'll pull the tracking numbers for a few of those checkout calls and get engineering on it. Can you send me one example call ID?

22
00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:35.373
Vanessa Grant: Yeah, you know, I'll dig one up after this.

23
00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:38.997
Tom Lindqvist: Perfect. Anything else on the tracking side, or...?

24
00:02:39.737 --> 00:02:42.897
Vanessa Grant: No, that's the main thing. Attribution's been fine otherwise.

25
00:02:44.158 --> 00:02:47.552
Tom Lindqvist: Good. And PreSense, still popping the journey for agents?

26
00:02:48.796 --> 00:02:50.145
Vanessa Grant: Yep, no complaints there.

27
00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:59.316
Tom Lindqvist: Great. So what I'll do is open a ticket with the details, um, loop in our tracking team, and keep you posted.

28
00:02:59.316 --> 00:03:01.814
Tom Lindqvist: Probably early next week for an update.

29
00:03:02.642 --> 00:03:13.975
Vanessa Grant: Sounds good. One more um, thing, uh, unrelated. We're onboarding a new batch of agents in November, eight of them. Do I need to do anything on the Invoca seat side?

30
00:03:14.646 --> 00:03:21.837
Tom Lindqvist: Just send me their emails and I'll get them provisioned. No charge since you're under your seat count.

31
00:03:22.047 --> 00:03:29.476
Vanessa Grant: Perfect. Oh, and tell your team the AI Voice Agent's been a nice surprise. Callers actually use it.

32
00:03:29.838 --> 00:03:34.887
Tom Lindqvist: Ha, I'll pass that along. Alright, I'll get that ticket moving. Talk soon.

33
00:03:36.362 --> 00:03:37.623
Vanessa Grant: Thanks, Tom. Bye.
